---
title: Toucan Touchpad Gesture State Machine
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR

    [*] --> INACTIVE

    %% ── Transitions from INACTIVE ──────────────────────────────────────────────

    INACTIVE --> TAP_PENDING   : contact [not rim or right half]
    INACTIVE --> SCROLL_ACTIVE : contact [rim AND left half]

    %% ── Transitions from TAP_PENDING ───────────────────────────────────────────

    TAP_PENDING --> MOVING      : tap_timeout fires [contact]
    TAP_PENDING --> DRAG_WINDOW : tap_timeout fires [lift]
    TAP_PENDING --> DRAGGING    : contact [z ≥ FORCE_DRAG_Z_THRESHOLD] (hard press)

    %% ── Transitions from MOVING ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    MOVING --> INACTIVE  : lift
    MOVING --> DRAGGING  : contact [z ≥ FORCE_DRAG_Z_THRESHOLD] (hard press, always left)

    %% ── Transitions from DRAG_WINDOW ───────────────────────────────────────────

    DRAG_WINDOW --> DRAGGING_PENDING : contact [z ≥ DOUBLE_CLICK_DRAG_Z_THRESHOLD]
    DRAG_WINDOW --> TAP_PENDING      : contact [z < DOUBLE_CLICK_DRAG_Z_THRESHOLD]
    DRAG_WINDOW --> INACTIVE         : drag_window_timeout fires

    %% ── Transitions from DRAGGING_PENDING ──────────────────────────────────────

    DRAGGING_PENDING --> INACTIVE : lift [before timeout] (Double Tap)
    DRAGGING_PENDING --> DRAGGING : drag_pending_timeout fires [contact]

    %% ── Transitions from DRAGGING ──────────────────────────────────────────────

    DRAGGING --> DRAG_JUMP : lift [at drag-jump rim]
    DRAGGING --> INACTIVE  : lift [not at drag-jump rim]

    %% ── Transitions from DRAG_JUMP ─────────────────────────────────────────────

    DRAG_JUMP --> DRAGGING : contact
    DRAG_JUMP --> INACTIVE : drag_jump_timeout fires

    %% ── Transitions from SCROLL_ACTIVE ─────────────────────────────────────────

    SCROLL_ACTIVE --> SCROLL_DEAD : contact [in dead zone]
    SCROLL_ACTIVE --> INACTIVE    : lift

    %% ── Transitions from SCROLL_DEAD ───────────────────────────────────────────

    SCROLL_DEAD --> SCROLL_ACTIVE : contact [outside dead zone]
    SCROLL_DEAD --> INACTIVE      : lift


    note left of INACTIVE
        Finger: up · Button: none · Timers: all idle
        pad_off timer may still be pending (PAD layer stays ON)
        ──────────────────────────────────────────
        → contact [scroll rim AND left half]:
            cancel pad_off timer
            scroll_ref_x/y ← current
            scroll_clicks_rem ← 0
            scroll_direction ← lower half → H, upper half → V
            emit BTN_TOUCH=1  [PAD ON]
        → contact [else]:
            cancel pad_off timer
            is_left ← x > X_RCLICK_MIN
            touch_start_x/y ← current
            prev_scaled_x/y ← current
            schedule tap_timeout
            emit BTN_TOUCH=1  [PAD ON]
        → pad_off timer fires:
            emit BTN_TOUCH=0  [PAD OFF]
        ──────────────────────────────────────────
        Zone order (checked first-match):
          RIM+LEFT  scroll rim AND left half AND y not in scroll exclusion band → scroll
          RIGHT-CLICK  x ≤ X_RCLICK_MIN          → is_left=false
          PRIMARY   everything else              → is_left=true
        Scroll exclusion band: y ∈ [PAD_CENTER±excl_half]
          where excl_half = 1024 × scroll_exclusion_zone_percent / 100 / 2
    end note

    note right of TAP_PENDING
        Finger: down · Button: none
        Timer: tap_timeout armed
        Per-packet: cursor movement SUPPRESSED
        prev_scaled_x/y stays at touch_start
        ──────────────────────────────────────────
        → tap_timeout [contact]:
            if tap-snap: prev_scaled_x/y ← current
            [enter MOVING]
            first MOVING packet emits delta from prev_scaled
        → tap_timeout [lift]:
            emit is_left ? BTN_0=1 : BTN_1=1  (button down)
            schedule drag_window_timeout
            [enter DRAG_WINDOW — PAD stays ON]
        → contact [z ≥ FORCE_DRAG_Z_THRESHOLD]:
            cancel tap_timeout
            emit is_left ? BTN_0=1 : BTN_1=1  (button down, sync)
            prev_scaled_x/y ← current  (snap)
            [enter DRAGGING — PAD stays ON]
    end note

    note right of MOVING
        Finger: down · Button: none
        Per-packet: emit REL_X, REL_Y
            delta = current - prev_scaled_x/y
            prev_scaled_x/y ← current
        ──────────────────────────────────────────
        → lift:
            schedule pad_off timer  [deferred PAD OFF]
        → contact [z ≥ FORCE_DRAG_Z_THRESHOLD]:
            is_left ← true  (always left for force-drag)
            prev_scaled_x/y ← current  (snap)
            emit BTN_0=1  (left button down, sync)
            [enter DRAGGING — PAD stays ON]
    end note

    note right of DRAG_WINDOW
        Finger: UP · Button: HELD (is_left → BTN_0, else BTN_1)
        Timer: drag_window_timeout armed
        Waiting for re-touch to begin drag
        ──────────────────────────────────────────
        → contact [z ≥ DOUBLE_CLICK_DRAG_Z_THRESHOLD]:
            emit is_left ? BTN_0=0 : BTN_1=0  (release, sync)
            prev_scaled_x/y ← current
            cancel drag_window_timeout
            schedule drag_pending_timeout
            [enter DRAGGING_PENDING — PAD stays ON]
        → contact [z < DOUBLE_CLICK_DRAG_Z_THRESHOLD]:
            emit is_left ? BTN_0=0 : BTN_1=0  (release, sync)
            cancel drag_window_timeout
            recompute is_left ← x > X_RCLICK_MIN
            touch_start_x/y ← current
            prev_scaled_x/y ← current
            schedule tap_timeout
            [enter TAP_PENDING — PAD stays ON]
        → drag_window_timeout:
            emit is_left ? BTN_0=0 : BTN_1=0  (release, sync)
            schedule pad_off timer  [deferred PAD OFF]
    end note

    note right of DRAGGING_PENDING
        Finger: down · Button: none
        Timer: drag_pending_timeout armed
        Per-packet: cursor movement SUPPRESSED
        ──────────────────────────────────────────
        → lift [before timeout]:
            cancel drag_pending_timeout
            emit is_left ? BTN_0=1 : BTN_1=1  (button down, sync)
            schedule tap_click_work (button up after 60ms)
            schedule pad_off timer  [deferred PAD OFF]
            [enter INACTIVE]  (Double Tap)
        → drag_pending_timeout [contact]:
            if tap-snap: prev_scaled_x/y ← current
            emit is_left ? BTN_0=1 : BTN_1=1  (button down, sync)
            [enter DRAGGING — PAD stays ON]
    end note

    note right of DRAGGING
        Finger: down · Button: HELD (per is_left)
        Per-packet: emit REL_X, REL_Y
            delta = current - prev_scaled_x/y
            prev_scaled_x/y ← current
        ──────────────────────────────────────────
        → lift [last position at drag-jump rim]:
            schedule drag_jump_timeout
            [enter DRAG_JUMP — PAD stays ON, button stays held]
        → lift [last position not at drag-jump rim]:
            emit is_left ? BTN_0=0 : BTN_1=0  (release, sync)
            schedule pad_off timer  [deferred PAD OFF]
    end note

    note right of DRAG_JUMP
        Finger: UP · Button: HELD (per is_left)
        Timer: drag_jump_timeout armed
        User repositioning finger across pad
        ──────────────────────────────────────────
        → contact:
            prev_scaled_x/y ← current  (snap)
            cancel drag_jump_timeout
            [enter DRAGGING — PAD stays ON]
        → drag_jump_timeout:
            emit is_left ? BTN_0=0 : BTN_1=0  (release, sync)
            schedule pad_off timer  [deferred PAD OFF]
    end note

    note right of SCROLL_ACTIVE
        Finger: down · Button: none
        scroll_direction set on entry (retained through SCROLL_DEAD):
            lower half → HORIZONTAL (REL_HWHEEL)
            upper half → VERTICAL   (REL_WHEEL)
        Per-packet:
            dot = ref_x·cx + ref_y·cy  (centred coords)
            det = ref_x·cy − ref_y·cx
            ang = atan2_16(det, dot)
            scroll_clicks_rem += ang · WHEEL_CLICKS
            emit whole clicks; keep remainder
            scroll_ref_x/y ← current
        ──────────────────────────────────────────
        → contact [in dead zone]:
            [enter SCROLL_DEAD — scroll_direction kept]
        → lift:
            scroll_clicks_rem ← 0
            schedule pad_off timer  [deferred PAD OFF]
    end note

    note right of SCROLL_DEAD
        Finger: down · Button: none
        Entered when finger crosses pad centre
        Per-packet: scroll SUPPRESSED
        scroll_direction retained for resume
        ──────────────────────────────────────────
        → contact [outside dead zone]:
            scroll_ref_x/y ← current  (reset reference)
            [enter SCROLL_ACTIVE — same scroll_direction]
        → lift:
            schedule pad_off timer  [deferred PAD OFF]
    end note
